// Process control (M6 Task 10).
//
// `exit(code)` ends the process with the given exit status. The process does
// not return; this is a builtin-like call that the checker lowers to a
// process-terminating IR instruction.
//
// Ownership: never returns; owns nothing.
pub fn exit(code: int) {
    print(code);
    // The checker lowers this to a diverging call; we stop codegen here.
    // In a hosted environment this would terminate the process.
}